            <h2>Airlines Flying from Seattle to Maui</h2>
            <h3>Full-Service Airlines</h3>
            <h4>Alaska Airlines</h4>
            <p>As the hometown carrier of the Pacific Northwest and the dominant operator of nonstop service between Seattle and Maui, Alaska leverages its Sea-Tac hub to anchor this transpacific corridor with multiple daily frequencies and an intimate understanding of Northwest traveler expectations.</p>
            <p><b>Highlights:</b></p>
            <ul>
                <li>Multiple daily nonstop flights on Boeing 737-800, 737-900ER, and 737 MAX 9 aircraft, offering consistent product across the fleet</li>
                <li>Mileage Plan earning with valuable elite status tiers, generous partner redemption opportunities with Emirates and Qantas, and the famous Companion Fare</li>
                <li>Multiple cabin experiences spanning Economy, Premium Class (extra legroom, priority boarding), and First Class with premium dining and West Coast craft beverages</li>
                <li>Strong Pacific network providing seamless onward connections and alternative routing through Portland, San Diego, and Anchorage.</li>
                <li>Partnership with Hawaiian Airlines for inter-island connections and reciprocal earning from Kahului to Kona, Lihue, and Honolulu</li>
                <li>Extensive Pacific Northwest feed from Spokane, Bellingham, Portland, and Boise enabling single-ticket Maui access through Seattle</li>
            </ul>
            <h4>Delta Air Lines</h4>
            <p>Delta operates robust nonstop service from its Seattle hub to Maui, leveraging its growing Pacific presence and operational reliability to capture tech-sector and corporate travelers.</p>
            <p><b>Advantages:</b></p>
            <ul>
                <li>Daily nonstop flights on Boeing 767-300ER and Airbus A321neo aircraft, offering wide-body comfort on select departures</li>
                <li>SkyMiles earning with Medallion qualifying segments and dollars toward elite tier status.</li>
                <li>Delta One business class with fully flat seats, premium dining, and Westin Heavenly Inflight bedding on wide-body configured aircraft</li>
                <li>Comfort+ and Premium Select options providing incremental upgrades for taller passengers and frequent flyers</li>
                <li>Strong codeshare and inter-island connections through Hawaiian Airlines partnership</li>
                <li>Reliable operational metrics and proactive rebooking during irregular operations, particularly important for vacation-sensitive itineraries</li>
            </ul>
            <h4>Hawaiian Airlines</h4>
            <p>The Aloha State's flag carrier brings authentic island hospitality to the Pacific Northwest, offering a cultural bridge that begins before wheels leave the tarmac at Sea-Tac.</p>
            <p><b>Benefits include:</b></p>
            <ul>
                <li>Daily nonstop flights aboard Airbus A321neo and A330-200 aircraft with island-inspired cabin design and crew trained in Hawaiian cultural protocols</li>
                <li>HawaiianMiles earning with Pualani elite status, companion fare discounts, and valuable partner redemption opportunities</li>
                <li>Extra Comfort seating offering priority boarding, enhanced legroom, and personal power outlets at a moderate upgrade cost</li>
                <li>Complimentary island-inspired meals even in Main Cabin, featuring Hawaiian sweet bread, island-style entrees, and tropical beverages</li>
                <li>Strong cultural immersion from boarding through descent, with Hawaiian language announcements, island music, and lei-inspired cabin aesthetics</li>
            </ul>
            <h4>Southwest Airlines</h4>
            <p>The Dallas-based low-cost giant serves the Seattle-Maui market with competitive fares and the industry's most passenger-friendly baggage policy, resonating strongly with families and outdoor adventurers.</p>
            <p><b>Advantages:</b></p>
            <ul>
                <li>Daily nonstop service aboard Boeing 737 MAX 8 aircraft certified for extended over-water ETOPS operations</li>
                <li>Rapid Rewards earning with Companion Pass eligibility, A-List priority boarding, and no blackout dates on award redemptions</li>
                <li>Two free checked bags on every fare, a transformative advantage for surfers hauling boards, golfers with club sets, and families packing snorkel gear for a week in Kihei</li>
                <li>No change fees and no cancellation penalties, providing flexibility when Puget Sound storms or Maui's trade winds disrupt schedules</li>
                <li>Open seating policy allowing groups to sit together without advance seat selection surcharges</li>
                <li>Extensive connecting network through Seattle for travelers originating across the Pacific Northwest and Mountain West</li>
            </ul>
            <h4>United Airlines</h4>
            <p>United connects Seattle-Maui passengers through its San Francisco, Denver, and Los Angeles hubs, with San Francisco offering the most direct coastal routing to the Valley Isle.</p>
            <p><b>Features:</b></p>
            <ul>
                <li>MileagePlus earning with Premier qualifying credits and lifetime miles accumulation.</li>
                <li>Polaris Business Class with lie-flat beds, Saks Fifth Avenue bedding, and premium dining on long-haul configured aircraft from SFO</li>
                <li>Star Alliance membership providing global lounge access and reciprocal benefits.</li>
                <li>Strong connecting schedule through San Francisco with onward nonstop service to Kahului</li>
            </ul>
            <h4>American Airlines</h4>
            <p>American routes Seattle-Maui passengers through its Phoenix and Los Angeles hubs, with Phoenix offering the most direct southwestern routing to Kahului.</p>
            <p><b>Benefits:</b></p>
            <ul>
                <li>AAdvantage mileage earning with elite qualifying dollars, segments, and lifetime miles accumulation</li>
                <li>Multiple cabin experiences spanning Main Cabin, Main Cabin Extra, Premium Economy, and Flagship Business on wide-body aircraft</li>
                <li>oneworld alliance membership providing global lounge access and reciprocal benefits</li>
                <li>Strong connecting schedule through Phoenix with favorable weather reliability during Seattle's stormy winter months</li>
            </ul>
            <h3>Low-Cost Options</h3>
            <p>No ultra-low-cost carrier currently operates nonstop from Seattle to Maui. Spirit and Frontier serve SEA for mainland destinations but do not cross the Pacific. Budget travelers monitor Southwest sales and legacy carrier promotional fares, particularly during shoulder season.</p>
            <p>Inter-island budget carriers serving Maui:</p>
            <ul>
                <li><b>Southwest -</b> Expanding inter-island network connecting Kahului to Honolulu, Kona, and Lihue</li>
                <li><b>Mokulele Airlines - </b> Commuter service from Kahului to Kapalua, Hana, and Molokai using small turboprop aircraft</li>
            </ul>
            <h2>Seasonal Variations</h2>
            <h3>Peak Season: December to March and June to August</h3>
            <p>Highest demand with corresponding premium pricing.</p>
            <p><b>During peak months:</b></p>
            <ul>
                <li>Airfares reach annual highs, particularly Christmas week, New Year's, Presidents' Day weekend, and mid-July</li>
                <li>Alaska and Delta operate multiple daily nonstops, sometimes adding additional seasonal capacity</li>
                <li>Southwest and Hawaiian maintain daily nonstop service with peak-season frequency increases</li>
                <li>Resort rates in Wailea, Kaanapali, and Kapalua reach premium levels with minimum stay requirements</li>
                <li>Rental car inventory sells out months in advance, particularly for convertibles, jeeps, and SUVs suited to the Road to Hana and Upcountry exploration</li>
                <li>Popular activities including Haleakalā sunrise reservations, Molokini snorkeling tours, and Old Lahaina Luau require booking</li>
                <li>Restaurant availability becomes challenging at waterfront establishments in Lahaina, Paia, and Kihei</li>
            </ul>
            <p><b>Premium pricing periods:</b></p>
            <ul>
                <li><b>December 20 through January 5 - </b> absolute peak as Seattleites escape perpetual darkness, rain, and post-holiday blues</li>
                <li><b>Presidents' Day and MLK Day weekends -</b>  short-break demand from Seattle, Tacoma, and Bellevue</li>
                <li><b>February - </b> peak of Seattle's gray season drives maximum demand for tropical sun</li>
                <li><b>June through August -</b>  family travel aligned with Washington school schedules</li>
                <li><b>Thanksgiving week - </b> popular pre-holiday tropical escape</li>
            </ul>
            <h3>Shoulder Season: April to May and September to November</h3>
            <p>Most balanced Maui experience with pleasant weather and manageable crowds.</p>
            <p><b>Advantages:</b></p>
            <ul>
                <li>Economy fares typically 20-35% below December peaks</li>
                <li>Temperatures in the 70s to 80s°F with reliable trade winds and occasional light showers on the windward side</li>
                <li>Better availability at boutique hotels, vacation rentals, and resort properties</li>
                <li>Smaller crowds at Haleakalā National Park, Iao Valley, and the Maui Ocean Center</li>
                <li>Ideal conditions for exploring the Upcountry region, visiting lavender farms in Kula, and wine tasting at Ulupalakua Ranch</li>
                <li>Shoulder season surf on the north shore begins building in September and October</li>
            </ul>
            <h3>Off-Season: Late August to October (excluding Labor Day)</h3>
            <p>Late summer and early autumn offer value before winter demand surges.</p>
            <p><b>Benefits:</b></p>
            <ul>
                <li>Lowest airfares of the year - economy round-trips frequently $350-$600</li>
                <li>Reduced tourist presence at major beaches and attractions</li>
                <li>Hotel rates at annual lows with promotional packages and resort credits</li>
                <li>Warm ocean temperatures ideal for snorkeling, diving, and beginner surfing</li>
                <li>Hurricane season runs June through November, though direct hits on Maui are rare; travel insurance recommended</li>
            </ul>
            <p><b>Considerations:</b></p>
            <ul>
                <li>Higher humidity and occasional tropical showers, particularly on the windward coast near Hana and Keanae</li>
                <li>Some resort restaurants and activities reduce hours in late August and September</li>
                <li>Hurricane season requires flexible planning and comprehensive travel insurance</li>
            </ul>
