                    <li><b>South Satellite (S Gates) - </b> International arrivals and departures for Delta, Hawaiian, and international carriers with customs and immigration facilities</li>
                </ul>
                <h4>Transportation to Seattle-Tacoma International</h4>
                <ul>
                    <li><b> Link Light Rail - </b> Connects downtown Seattle, Capitol Hill, University of Washington, and Angle Lake to the airport; cost approximately $3.25-$3.50; journey time 38 minutes from Westlake Center.</li>
                    <li><b> Taxi and Rideshare - </b> Uber, Lyft, and traditional taxis serve all terminals; $35-$55 to downtown depending on traffic and surge</li>
                    <li><b> Driving and Parking - </b> Multiple parking garages adjacent to terminals; economy lots with shuttle service; cell phone waiting lots for pickups</li>
                    <li><b> King County Metro Bus -</b>  Routes 124 and 156 connect Burien, Tukwila, and Renton to the airport.</li>
                </ul>
                <h4>Lounges at Seattle-Tacoma International</h4>
                <ul>
                    <li>Alaska Lounge (Concourse C and North Satellite) - multiple locations for Alaska premium passengers and Mileage Plan elites</li>
                    <li>Delta Sky Club (Concourse A and South Satellite)</li>
                    <li>United Club (Concourse A)</li>
                    <li>American Airlines Admirals Club (Concourse D)</li>
                    <li>The Club at SEA (Concourse A and South Satellite) - independent lounge accessible via Priority Pass and other programs</li>
                </ul>
